/**
 * challenges.ts — overlays (cookie consent, modals, interstitials) and captcha solving for the browser MCP (2026-10-20).
 * Operator order: "finish out the challenge / captcha testing to isolate the best method … and other challenges agents will need to be able
 * to solve, fill out, or click through". Evidence: omniclaude-v4/.cortex/research/captcha-bakeoff-2026-10-20.md (§1–§4).
 *
 * Design — compose what the MCP already has, add typed decisions where pixels must be read:
 *   dismiss_overlays : DOM first (known consent-manager selectors, then a generic overlay heuristic), per frame, policy-driven. No model.
 *   solve_captcha    : iframe geometry from the main document (works on both backends), a region screenshot, ONE typed MENU read of the
 *                      instruction (class × grid × mode — a decision model reads menus perfectly, spells nothing), per-tile nouls in one
 *                      Jev request (85% exact grids in the bake-off), human-like clicks, re-read until no tile matches, Verify, typed
 *                      "is it solved" noul. "Click the X" prompts use Jev Box. Open-vocabulary prompts fall back to the driving model.
 * Pure helpers here are unit-tested (challenges.test.ts); the Durable Object (mcp.ts) owns page state.
 */

